# SimLight V2 — Decision-Driven Microsimulation Architecture & Implementation Plan

This plan establishes the architecture and implementation roadmap for **SimLight V2**, transforming SimLight from an assessment/quiz platform into a **decision-consequence simulation engine** with an intuitive faculty authoring layer and an executive-level student simulation experience.

---

## 1. Architectural Transformation (V1 vs V2)

| Dimension | SimLight V1 (Current) | SimLight V2 (Proposed) |
|---|---|---|
| **Core Paradigm** | Quiz / Assessment (Read text → Answer MCQ/Text/Blank) | **Microsimulation (Situation → Decision → Rule → Consequence → New State)** |
| **Pacing** | Fixed 3 Phases | **Dynamic Rounds (1 to 15 rounds)** |
| **State** | Static text + points score + static budget/risk meters | **Live Variables & KPIs (Cash, Inventory, Demand, Satisfaction, Reliability, Margin)** |
| **Student Input** | MCQ, Free text, Formula, Fill-in-blanks | **8 Decision Components: Select, Allocate, Slider, Quantity, Ranking, Budget, Portfolio, Negotiation** |
| **Engine** | Question correct/incorrect grading & AI text feedback | **Deterministic Rule & Consequence Engine (WHEN / IF ... THEN ...) with Trade-Offs** |
| **Dynamics** | Linear event sequence | **Triggered & Probabilistic Events (disruptions, tariffs, demand surges)** |
| **Learning Evaluation** | % Score on questions | **Business Performance Scorecard + Decision History Audit + What-If / Replay Mode** |
| **Faculty Role** | Writing questions & answers | **Simulation Architect: Canva + Excel + ChatGPT no-code world builder** |

